ns to start in the fall of 2027. This position is for the undergraduate, face-to-face position, which takes place on the campus and in the community. Faculty members will be responsible for providing effective learning in the classroom, clinical and/or laboratory. All faculty members must have experience in the clinical area of their expertise and will be required to facilitate experiences for students in the clinical setting/outside agencies. The role of the faculty also requires dedication and commitment to  service at the department and university organizational levels, student advising in all levels of the program, mentorship engagement, and participation in annual scholarly endeavors. Active engagement in development and evaluation of program curriculum, outcomes, and policies; as well as maintenance and oversight of accreditation standards are essential obligations. Regular attendance at department and university events and functions is an expectation of all full-time faculty. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Master's degree in Nursing. Eligible for RN licensure in Massachusetts. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Nursing Teaching experience in higher education and experience with web-enhanced and online teaching is preferred. Active program of research/ scholarship is highly desired. Experience and expertise across varied curriculum areas in respective clinical areas are strongly preferred. Additional Information: This is a full-time, benefited, exempt position. Salary is commensurate with experience and discipline, with a minimum established by the Appendix O of the MSCA contract. The anticipated start date for this position is September 1, 2027. Here at Worcester State University, it is strongly recommended that all employees be vaccinated against COVID-19 before they begin employment. Worcester State University offers a competitive benefits package that includes: a choice of 8 different pre-taxed, health insurance plan options pension and supplemental plan retirement options life insurance up to 8x the annual salary long-term disability coverage dental insurance 10 sick days accrued per year 2 personal days per year paid holidays Free on-campus gym access. tuition remission for self, spouse, and dependent children and more... We are an equal opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. M/F/D/V. Members of traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online and may do so by visiting www.worcester.edu/careers , and submitting the following documents: Letter of Interest CV Statement of Teaching Philosophy Contact information for three professional references (letters of recommendation will be requested for selected candidates at a later date). We are an equal opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. M/F/D/V. Members of traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply. For assistance with uploading materials, log a ticket via the HelpDesk link, or contact us directly at 508-929-8053. URL: www.worcester.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
