 Occupational Studies/Master of Occupational Therapy Program beginning September 2027. Additional teaching may be available during the summer semesters. This position includes teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, advising, research, scholarship, and ongoing involvement in Department and University committees. Interprofessional classroom experiences and research projects with other academic departments are highly encouraged. Requirements: Required Qualifications: A research-based terminal degree or ABD is preferred; Certification by NBCOT; At least 5 years of clinical experience as an occupational therapist; and be eligible for licensure as an OTR in Massachusetts. Demonstration of clinical expertise and teaching with a focus on mental health and/or gerontology in various contexts. Previous teaching experience in higher education is preferred. Additional Information: This is a full-time, benefited, exempt position. Salary is commensurate with experience and discipline, with a minimum established by the Appendix O of the MSCA contract. The anticipated start date for this position is September 1, 2027. Here at Worcester State University, it is strongly recommended that all employees be vaccinated against COVID-19 before they begin employment. Worcester State University offers a competitive benefits package that includes: a choice of 8 different pre-taxed, health insurance plan options pension and supplemental plan retirement options life insurance up to 8x the annual salary long-term disability coverage dental insurance 10 sick days accrued per year 2 personal days per year paid holidays Free on-campus gym access. tuition remission for self, spouse, and dependent children and more... We are an equal opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. M/F/D/V. Members of traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply. Application Instructions: Initial screening of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Th