rculation Desk. The part-time library assistant position is a non-benefitted position. Responsibilities: Supervises part-time student workers Renews and discharges library materials Helps users locate and use materials Opens and closes the library Manages library collections by inventorying, shifting, shelf-reading and barcoding Assists with interlibrary loan processing Works on special projects Collects fines Performs other duties as assigned Requirements: Required Qualifications: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Outstanding customer services skills Attention to detail Experience using Microsoft Office applications Associates degree or equivalent college experience Preferred Qualifications: Previous customer service experience Previous experience working within libraries Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. This is a part-time, non-benefited, hourly position. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online at worcester.interviewexchange.com. A representative from the department will contact individuals for interviews. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
