esponsible for providing professional, safe, and engaging fitness instruction and wellness support to participants and clients. Employees in this role are expected to foster a welcoming, inclusive, service-oriented environment while promoting participant safety, well-being, and positive experiences within the Recreation & Wellness programs and facilities. Responsibilities: Provide a welcoming, inclusive, and safe fitness experience for all participants and clients. Conduct group exercise classes and personal training sessions in accordance with Wellness Center protocols and industry standards to promote a positive participant experience. Incorporate an appropriate warm up, class routine/session workout, including a cool down/ stretch period. Utilize appropriate and professional music selections when applicable Instruct and train within the scope of knowledge, certification, and expertise. Monitor participant and client safety throughout all classes and training sessions. Prepare, set up, and break down exercise spaces and equipment as needed. Assist with participant and client check-in procedures when applicable. Properly operate and maintain sound and audio equipment when applicable. Report all safety concerns, incidents, and equipment maintenance issues promptly to supervisors. Adhere to all Recreation & Wellness. departmental policies, procedures, and expectations. Performs other duties as assigned. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Appropriate group fitness/personal training experience related to desired format. Current CPR/AED certification. Primary Group Fitness/Personal Training Certification from ACSM, ACE, AFAA, NETA or NASM preferred or other nationally recognized and accredited organization. Preferred Qualifications: Strong oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated interpersonal and customer service skills. Ability to foster a welcoming, inclusive, and participant focused environment Knowledge of fitness instruction principles, participant safety practices, and wellness industry standards. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online at worcester.interviewexchange.com. A representative from the department will contact individuals for interviews. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
