    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202128": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor (Part-time, Non-Benefited) 2 positions",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Academic Advisor (Part-time, Non-Benefited) 2 positions Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Academic Advisor (Part-time, Non-Benefited) 2 positions Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Academic Advisor (Part-time, Non-Benefited) 2 positions Category: Part-time Non-Benefited/Hourly Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Jul 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 202128 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: TITLE: Academic Advisor DEPARTMENT : Academic Success SUPERVISOR : Assistant Dean, Academic Success Center SCHEDULE: Up to 29 hours per week. General Statement of Duties: The Academic Success Center at Worcester State University seeks a student-centered and collaborative Part-Time Academic Advisor to provide academic advising and support services to undergraduate students across all disciplines. This position serves as a primary walk-in advisor, assisting students with academic planning, degree requirements, registration, major exploration, academic policies, and referrals to campus resources. The Part-Time Academic Advisor also serves as a key contact for students considering course withdrawals, University withdrawals, or leaves of absence, providing guidance, support, and assistance with the completion of required documentation. The successful candidate will possess strong interpersonal and communication skills, demonstrate sensitivity to diverse student needs, maintain confidentiality, and provide exceptional customer service in a fast-paced student services environment. This position requires in-person availability and does not include remote work. Responsibilities: Serve as a walk-in advisor to undergraduate students across all disciplines to answer general questions related to program and University requirements. Advise students regarding degree requirements, academic policies, registration procedures, academic standing, and University resources. Assist students with major exploration, academic planning, and referrals to faculty advisors and campus support services. Respond to student inquiries via email, phone, and in-person appointments. Serve as the primary contact for students considering course withdrawals, University withdrawals, or leaves of absence. Counsel students regarding available options and assist with the completion and processing of required documentation. Connect students with appropriate academic, financial, and personal support resources. Support Academic Success Center efforts related to student retention, persistence, and academic success. Maintain accurate records of student interactions and advising activities. Utilize student information systems and technologies including Colleague/Datatel, Self-Service, Starfish (Early Support), ImageNow, TES (Transfer Equivalency System), Accuplacer, and other University systems. Maintain working knowledge of University policies, academic regulations, transfer credit processes, and general education requirements. Provide guidance and oversight to student employees assigned to the Academic Success Center. Participate in departmental meetings, training, and professional development opportunities. Other duties as assigned. Requirements: Required Qualifications: 1. Bachelor's degree. 2. Experience working in higher education, student services, advising, counseling, or a related field. 3. Strong interpersonal, communication, presentation, active listening, and advising skills. 4. Ability to work effectively with a diverse population of students, faculty, staff, and community members. 5. Demonstrated ability to manage confidential information with professionalism, sensitivity, and discretion. 6. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple priorities. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Master's degree in Higher Education, Counseling, Student Affairs, or a related field. 2. Experience using student information systems and student success technologies such as Starfish, Colleague/Datatel, Self-Service, ImageNow, TES, Accuplacer, or similar platforms. 3. Experience supporting student retention, persistence, and academic success initiatives. 4. Experience working with students in transition, including first-year, transfer, and academically at-risk populations. Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. This is a part-time, non-benefited, hourly position. This position is fully in-person and requires regular interaction with students, faculty, staff, and visitors within the Academic Success Center. The schedule is 29 hours per week and may include participation in occasional evening or weekend programs related to orientation, registration, or student success initiatives. Hourly rate: $23/ hour Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online at worcester.interviewexchange.com. A representative from the department will contact individuals for interviews. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
