    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=192786": {
      "title": "Temporary Maintainer, Custodial Associate (Residence Halls)",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Temporary Maintainer, Custodial Associate (Residence Halls) Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Temporary Maintainer, Custodial Associate (Residence Halls) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Temporary Maintainer, Custodial Associate (Residence Halls) Category: Part-time Non-Benefited/Hourly Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: 352-Housing Services Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Sep 11, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 192786 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: OFFICIAL TITLE: Maintainer, Custodial Associate (Residence Halls) SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Maintenance Working Foreman and/or APA Supervisor General Statement of Duties: The Maintainer II, Custodial Associate is responsible for performing routine maintenance tasks related to the cleanliness and upkeep of university buildings and building walkways. Responsibilities: Cleans any/all areas of university buildings including but not limited to offices, classrooms, corridors, walls, floors, windows, furniture, woodwork, toilets, bathrooms, showers, locker rooms, fixtures, etc., by washing, sanitizing, waxing, buffing, sweeping, polishing, dusting, and vacuuming; meets the university's standard for cleanliness in performance of duties. Operates powered cleaning equipment including but not limited to buffers, vacuums, and power washers. Moves furniture and materials in accordance with proper lifting techniques, as necessary. Empties waste receptacles including but not limited to waste barrels, garbage cans, and recycling bins. May be responsible for operating university vehicles and disposing waste in dumpsters. Shovels snow to maintain clear building walkways and stairs; spreads salt and/or sand as necessary. Makes general repairs of a simple nature, including minor repairs to cleaning equipment and replacing light bulbs. Properly secures cleaning equipment, cleaning equipment storage rooms, classrooms, offices, and buildings after use and in accordance with Facilities Operations guidelines. Inspects assigned work area(s) and notifies supervisor of areas or items requiring attention, such as leaking faucets, broken latches, damaged paint, etc. Assists with delivering goods and moving materials when needed and as assigned. Performs all duties safely and responsibly. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Ability to understand and apply the rules, regulations, policies, procedures, specifications, standards, and guidelines governing assigned work. Ability to comprehend and communicate effectively in the English language. Ability to establish and maintain harmonious working relationships. Ability to stand and walk for long periods of time. Ability to lift and carry heavy objects, up to 50 pounds without assistance. Ability to climb and work on ladders and scaffolds. Ability to operate powered and non-powered cleaning equipment. Physical stamina and endurance. Ability to legally operate a motor vehicle; valid drivers' license required. Ability to exercise sound judgment. Ability to work well independently and in a team setting. Ability to work overtime. Ability to perform essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Ability to successfully pass a pre-employment physical, drug test, thorough background check, and CORI check. Preferred Qualifications: Strong work ethic and a willingness to learn. Experience in building custodial work. Valid Massachusetts hoisting license. Additional Information: *Appointment to this temporary position is contingent upon successful completion of pre-employment physical. Hourly Rate: $20.00- $25.00 Shift: 37.5 hours/ week, OT may be required. Days off: Saturday-Sunday. Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer, which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online at worcester.interviewexchange.com . A representative from the department will contact individuals for interviews. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=187604": {
      "title": "Academic Coach (Part-time, Non-Benefited)",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Academic Coach (Part-time, Non-Benefited) Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Academic Coach (Part-time, Non-Benefited) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Academic Coach (Part-time, Non-Benefited) Category: Part-time Non-Benefited/Hourly Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Apr 23, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 187604 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: TITLE: Skills Development Writing/Reading Comprehension Academic Coach for Multicultural Affairs DEPARTMENT : Multicultural Affairs SUPERVISOR : Director of Multicultural Affairs SSTA APPROVER: Director of Multicultural Affairs SCHEDULE: Position ends 9/20/25 General Statement of Duties: The Skills Development Writing/Reading Comprehension Academic Coach for Multicultural Affairs will primarily be responsible for administering student support as a Skills Development Academic Writing/Reading Comprehension Academic Coach for the Office of Multicultural Affairs (OMA). Skills Development writing/reading comprehension academic interventions include targeting students' literacy, fluency, study habits, time management skills, test-taking strategies, navigating systems, overall academic planning and goal setting, developing academic support engagement strategies and workshops, monitoring student academic learning, and addressing any academic challenges. The Office of Multicultural Affairs' mission is to increase access, retention, academic success, and graduation of our students who are from underrepresented backgrounds. In doing so, the incumbent will work with students from recruitment to the post-college experience, tracking students' progress using both qualitative and quantitative measurements. Responsibilities: 1. Provides individual/small group reading comprehension, writing, and academic instruction to OMA students, emphasizing comprehension strategies, vocabulary development, language comprehension, phonemic awareness, decoding, sentence construction cohesion, reasoning, writing mechanics, and fluency. 2. Assist students in developing the reading skills necessary for college-level coursework, standardized testing, and professional advancement. 3. Responsible for conducting relevant and appropriate intake assessments of students' needs and building curriculum and student support services to integrate literacy support into students' needs and strengths. 4. Assist in designing and implementing literacy workshops and interventions within the Office of Multicultural Affairs to address the needs of multilingual learners and underrepresented student populations. 5. Coordinates and leads Skills Development Workshop during the A.I.D. Summer Program 6. Coordinates and offers student support to OMA Vision Project students and OMA students taking summer courses. 7. Responsible for creating OMA reading/writing guides, materials, and resources to aid student learning 8. Co-chair Annual Martin Luther King Jr. Youth Breakfast Poetry Writing contest. 9. Collaborate with the OMA staff with university partners across divisions and the community to further develop, promote, and achieve program goals and objectives, including educational, multicultural student engagement, mentorship, co-curricular and leadership development opportunities inclusive of OMA Ambassadors, Women's Circle, Young Men's Group, First Generation Student Nation, Intercultural Student Alliance (ISA; formerly known as TWA), Women in STEM, and the Brotherhood-Sisterhood Leadership Conference. 10. Provide outreach to program participants, analyze data, and track student progress to tailor interventions and support student success. 11. Maintains accurate data, both qualitative and quantitative to measure the effectiveness of programming and to monitor students' progress; completes reports as necessary. 12. Assists the Director as necessary. 13. Demonstrates civility and professional, customer-service-oriented behavior worthy of emulation by other staff and students. 14. Responsible for contributing to the WSU Strategic Plan. 15. Responsible for contributing to Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action objectives. 16. Performs other duties as assigned. Requirements: Required Qualifications: 1. Bachelor's degree required 2. 3 or more years of related work experience teaching reading or literacy skills or a related field. 3. Experience with formal and informal reading and writing assessments 4. Experience working with multilingual learners and students from underrepresented backgrounds. 5. Excellent verbal and written communication skills; must be able to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, and administration. 6. Experience working in higher education settings. 7. Demonstrated knowledge and experience with educational student development and literacy instruction and interventions. 8. Knowledge of higher education principles, practices, and procedures. 9. Demonstrated experience with educational, cultural, and recreational programming. 10. Availability to work some off hours, including some Saturdays. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Master's degree Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. This is a part-time, non-benefited, hourly position. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online at worcester.interviewexchange.com. A representative from the department will contact individuals for interviews. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=201778": {
      "title": "Maintainer II, 3rd Shift (3 Positions)",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Maintainer II, 3rd Shift (3 Positions) Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Maintainer II, 3rd Shift (3 Positions) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Maintainer II, 3rd Shift (3 Positions) Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: 350-Facilities Operation Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Jun 22, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position ID: 201778 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: OFFICIAL TITLE: Maintainer II, Custodial Associate (3rd Shift) SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Maintenance Working Foreman and/or APA Supervisor SUPERVISION EXERCISED: None General Statement of Duties: The Maintainer II, Custodial Associate is responsible for performing routine maintenance tasks related to the cleanliness and upkeep of university buildings and building walkways. Responsibilities: (E) = Essential (E) Cleans any/all areas of university buildings including but not limited to offices, classrooms, corridors, walls, floors, windows, furniture, woodwork, toilets, bathrooms, showers, locker rooms, fixtures, etc., by washing, sanitizing, waxing, buffing, sweeping, polishing, dusting, and vacuuming; meets the university's standard for cleanliness in performance of duties. (E) Operates powered cleaning equipment including but not limited to buffers, vacuums, and power washers. (E) Moves furniture and materials in accordance with proper lifting techniques, as necessary. (E) Reviews inventory of cleaning supplies in work area(s) and requests/attains additional supplies as needed. (E) Empties waste receptacles including but not limited to waste barrels, garbage cans, and recycling bins. May be responsible for operating university vehicles and disposing waste in dumpsters. (E) Shovels snow to maintain clear building walkways and stairs; spreads salt and/or sand as necessary. (E) Makes general repairs of a simple nature, including minor repairs to cleaning equipment and replacing light bulbs. (E) Properly secures cleaning equipment, cleaning equipment storage rooms, classrooms, offices, and buildings after use and in accordance with Facilities Operations guidelines. (E) May be responsible for training new Maintainer II employees from time-to-time, as assigned. (E) Inspects assigned work area(s) and notifies supervisor of areas or items requiring attention, such as leaking faucets, broken latches, damaged paint, etc. (E) Periodically inspects cleaning equipment for wear and tear; notifies supervisor of concerns. (E) Assists with delivering goods and moving materials when needed and as assigned. (E) Serves as designated essential personnel; responds to weather and other emergency situations as assigned. (E) Performs all duties safely and responsibly. (E) Demonstrates civility and professional, customer-service oriented behavior, worthy of emulation by other staff and students. (E) Responsible for contributing to the WSU Strategic Plan. (E) Responsible for contributing to Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action objectives. Performs other duties as assigned within the Maintainer classification Classification specifications are available at http://www.mass.edu/foradmin/humanresources/classspecshrd.asp Requirements: Required Qualifications: Ability to understand and apply the rules, regulations, policies, procedures, specifications, standards, and guidelines governing assigned work. Ability to comprehend and communicate effectively in the English language. Ability to establish and maintain harmonious working relationships. Ability to stand and walk for long periods of time. Ability to lift and carry heavy objects, up to 50 pounds without assistance. Ability to climb and work on ladders and scaffolds. Ability to operate powered and non-powered cleaning equipment. Physical stamina and endurance. Ability to legally operate a motor vehicle; valid drivers' license required. Ability to exercise sound judgment. Ability to work well independently and in a team setting. Ability to work overtime. Ability to perform essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Ability to successfully pass a pre-employment physical, drug test, thorough background check, and CORI check. Preferred Qualifications: Strong work ethic and a willingness to learn. Experience in building custodial work. Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Here at Worcester State University, it is strongly recommended that all employees be vaccinated against COVID-19 before they begin employment. This is a grade 11, step 1 non-exempt, full-time (40 hours/week), benefited AFSCME position. The bi-weekly salary is $1,797.80 (annual salary is $46,742.80, plus shift differential). The shift is Sunday- Thursday, 11:00pm-7:00am. Worcester State University offers a competitive benefits package that includes: a choice of 8 different pre-taxed, health insurance plan options pension and supplemental plan retirement options life insurance up to 8x the annual salary long-term disability coverage dental insurance 10 vacation days accrued per year 15 sick days accrued per year 5 personal days per year paid holidays Free on-campus gym access. tuition remission for self, spouse, and dependent children and more... We are an equal opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. M/F/D/V. Members of traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online and may do so by visiting www.worcester.edu/careers, and submitting a cover letter, resume, and the contact information of three professional references. For assistance with uploading materials, log a ticket via the HelpDesk link, or contact us directly at 508-929-8053. URL: www.worcester.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205576": {
      "title": "Early Support Student Advocate (03 Student) 1 Position",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Early Support Student Advocate (03 Student) 1 Position Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Early Support Student Advocate (03 Student) 1 Position Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Early Support Student Advocate (03 Student) 1 Position Category: Student Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Oct 7, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 205576 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: TITLE: Early Support Student Advocate DEPARTMENT: Academic Success Center SUPERVISOR: Assistant Director of Early Support SCHEDULE: 6-8 hours per week General Statement of Duties: We are seeking a creative and motivated student to join the Academic Success Center team as an Early Support Student Advocate. In this role, you will be the primary student voice behind our Early Support Program - an online tool designed to connect students with academic, financial, and personal resources before challenges become overwhelming. The Early Support Advocate will help ensure every student knows how to access and use Early Support. This will be achieved primarily through a mix of creative social media posts/campaigns and in-person campus outreach. Key Responsibilities:  Social Media/Content Creation and Outreach Produce engaging content (Reels, TikToks, graphics, and stories) that explains what Early Support is and how students can use it. Manage the Early Support digital presence, including scheduling posts, interacting with student comments, and monitoring trends that resonate with the student body. Design promotional assets using Canva or similar tools for social media platforms and display boards when needed. Occasionally take part in campus tabling in high-traffic areas to pitch the Early Support program directly to peers, when available upon request. Assist in planning pop-up events at various times of the year to distribute Early Support information packets and items. Track online engagement metrics and get qualitative student feedback during in-person events. Requirements: Qualifications: Advanced understanding of Instagram video/reel creation, editing and basic graphic design (Canva experience preferred). Self-motivated with strong time-management skills and trustworthy to meet deadlines while working independently. Must be currently enrolled as an undergraduate student at Worcester State University in good academic standing. Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. *This position is available for WSU students only* Hourly Rate: $15.00 Application Instructions: Students must apply online. *This position is for WSU students only.* Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
