      "title": "Chandler the Lancer Mascot (03 Student) 1 Position",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Chandler the Lancer Mascot (03 Student) 1 Position Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Chandler the Lancer Mascot (03 Student) 1 Position Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Chandler the Lancer Mascot (03 Student) 1 Position Category: Student Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Oct 5, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 205517 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: TITLE: Chandler the Lancer Mascot DEPARTMENT: Athletics SUPERVISOR: Kelly Downs SCHEDULE: As needed General Statement of Duties: Chandler the Lancer must be an outgoing individual who work well with others, including children and fans of all ages. They must be in good physical condition to both wear heavy costumes and stand or walk for extended periods of time. Mascots must be able to read individuals' social cues to understand the level of interaction each fan may want. Ideal applicants for the position of mascot should be motivated in generating school or team spirit. Requirements: Qualifications: Mascots must develop the character of the mascot for the team. They must perform at most home games which are at night and or weekends, school events and charity events. They must work in conjunction with multiple departments. Mascots may also participate in the filming of on campus videos or promotional materials. They may also distribute promotional items, like T-shirts at special events. Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. *This position is available for WSU students only* Hourly Rate: $15.00 Application Instructions: Students must apply online. *This position is for WSU students only.* Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
