    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203587": {
      "title": "Student Access Assistant (03 Student) 2 positions",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Student Access Assistant (03 Student) 2 positions Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Student Access Assistant (03 Student) 2 positions Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Student Access Assistant (03 Student) 2 positions Category: Student Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Aug 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 203587 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: TITLE: Access Assistant DEPARTMENT: Student Accessibility Services SUPERVISOR: Rachel Graddy SCHEDULE: Hours vary according to student schedule General Statement of Duties/Responsibilities: The access assistant will attend specific classes and assist students with access needs in real-time. This may include sighted assistance: verbally describing worksheets, problems, and forms and assisting with their completion at the direction of the disabled student and/or physical assistance such as completing manual tasks based on the verbal instructions of the student. Whenever possible, the access assistant is responsible for taking comprehensive, typed notes throughout the class period. Requirements: Qualifications: Student in good academic standing. Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. *This position is available for WSU students only* Hourly Rate: $15.00 Application Instructions: Students must apply online. *This position is for WSU students only.* Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
