    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203179": {
      "title": "Residence Hall Desk Assistant (03 Student)",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Residence Hall Desk Assistant (03 Student) Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Residence Hall Desk Assistant (03 Student) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Residence Hall Desk Assistant (03 Student) Category: Student Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: 910-Residence Life Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Jul 30, 2026 Closes: Aug 3, 2027 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 203179 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: Position Summary The Residence Hall Desk Assistant (DA) serves as the first point of contact for students, guests, and visitors entering the residence halls. Desk Assistants play a vital role in creating a safe, secure, and welcoming residential community by monitoring building access, providing exceptional customer service, and supporting the daily operations of the Office of Residence Life. This position requires professionalism, reliability, sound judgment, and the ability to respond calmly and appropriately in a variety of situations. Requirements: Essential Responsibilities Building Safety & Security Monitor all traffic entering and exiting the residence hall. Verify identification for all individuals entering the residence halls. Conduct bag checks of all bags entering the residence halls in accordance with University policy. Manage the guest sign-in process and enforce the University's guest visitation policy. Notify Residence Life or University Police of policy violations, suspicious activity, or safety concerns. Report emergency situations immediately to Residence Life professional staff and/or University Police. Assist Residence Life and University Police during emergency or crisis situations. Customer Service Provide friendly, professional, and respectful customer service to residents, guests, and visitors. Answer questions and provide accurate information about Residence Life services and campus resources. Refer students to appropriate University offices when additional assistance is needed. Desk Operations Report to all scheduled shifts on time and remain on duty until properly relieved by the next Desk Assistant. Communicate important information, incidents, or concerns during shift change. Maintain accurate guest logs and other required desk documentation. Submit maintenance requests for issues identified in public areas. Report damage, theft, vandalism, or maintenance concerns to Residence Life professional staff. Professionalism Maintain familiarity with the Residence Hall Handbook, Residence Life policies, and University procedures. Build positive working relationships with Residence Life staff, University Police, Facilities, and fellow student employees. Demonstrate professionalism, integrity, confidentiality, and respect in all interactions. Serve as a positive role model within the residential community. Complete other duties and special projects as assigned. Employment Expectations Desk Assistants are expected to: Attend all required training sessions, staff meetings, and in-service programs. Maintain reliable attendance and arrive on time for every scheduled shift. Notify supervisors immediately of emergencies or circumstances affecting scheduled work. Maintain confidentiality regarding student information in accordance with University policy and FERPA. Exercise sound judgment and appropriately refer any situations beyond the scope of the position. Dress appropriately and present a professional appearance while on duty. Refrain from using personal devices in ways that interfere with job responsibilities. Be attentive, engaged, and actively monitoring the residence hall throughout the entire shift. Work collaboratively with fellow Desk Assistants, Resident Assistants, professional staff, and University Police. Be available to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and during University breaks as needed. Maintain eligibility for student employment throughout the duration of employment. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must: Be enrolled as a full-time Worcester State University student. Maintain a cumulative Worcester State University GPA of 2.5 or higher. Be in good academic and judicial standing with Worcester State University and the Office of Residence Life. Demonstrate strong communication, customer service, and interpersonal skills. Be dependable, organized, and able to work independently. Successfully complete all required employment paperwork and University training. Preferred Qualifications Preference may be given to applicants who demonstrate: Previous customer service or student leadership experience. Strong problem-solving and conflict resolution skills. The ability to remain calm and professional in stressful situations. Experience working with diverse populations. Additional Information: Additional Information Residence Hall Desk Assistant positions are filled throughout the academic year as vacancies occur. Applications will remain active in the hiring pool and will be reviewed as positions become available. Applicants who are no longer interested in employment are encouraged to withdraw their application. Continued employment is contingent upon maintaining all eligibility requirements, satisfactory job performance, and adherence to University and Residence Life policies. Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a diverse, equitable, and inclusive community. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203158": {
      "title": "Residence Life Office Assistant (03 Student)",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Residence Life Office Assistant (03 Student) Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Residence Life Office Assistant (03 Student) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Residence Life Office Assistant (03 Student) Category: Student Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: 910-Residence Life Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Jul 29, 2026 Closes: Aug 3, 2027 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: PT No Benefits Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $15.00 - $15.00 Position ID: 203158 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: Department : Residence Life and Housing Supervisor: Residence Life Professional Staff Member Hours: Up to 18.5 hours per week (primarily days and evenings) Pay Rate: $15.00/hour Position Summary The Residence Life Office Assistant (OA) serves as a primary point of contact for students, visitors, and university personnel entering the Residence Life Office. This role provides essential administrative support, customer service, and operational assistance to maintain a welcoming, efficient, and well-organized office environment. This position requires professionalism, reliability, sound judgment, and the ability to respond calmly and appropriately in a variety of situations. Requirements: Essential Responsibilities Customer Service & Administrative Support Front Desk Operations: Welcome students, family members, faculty, and visitors with a friendly, professional approach. Communication Management: Answer incoming calls, address inquiries, monitor voicemails, and route messages efficiently. Information & Referrals: Provide accurate information regarding residence hall policies or direct inquiries to appropriate university departments. Mail & Package Handling: Sort and distribute incoming mail and packages for office staff and residents. Office Maintenance: Maintain a tidy, professional, and well-stocked office space. Distribute supplies (e.g., trash bags, toilet paper, carts) to residents as needed. Operations & Safety Access & Lockouts: Assist residents with temporary key or access procedures during lockouts following established protocols. Facilities & Work Orders: Inspect public areas for maintenance needs and submit work orders promptly. Conference Support: Assist with conference setup and breakdown, including resident check-in/check-out, signage, trash removal, and linen handling. Emergency Assistance: Collaborate with Residence Life professional staff, student staff, and University Police during emergency or crisis situations. Report any damage, theft, or urgent incidents immediately. Office Continuity & Teamwork Shift Handover: Maintain strict punctuality for all assigned shifts and conduct thorough handovers to incoming staff, updating them on key activity, incidents, or pending tasks. Independent Execution: Work effectively both independently and as part of a team, utilizing MS Office, Google Workspace, and university-specific software applications. Qualifications & Core Competencies Academic Standing: Maintain an overall Worcester State University GPA of 2.0 or higher. Conduct Record: Be in good judicial standing with both the Office of Residence Life and Worcester State University. Interpersonal Skills: Strong verbal and written communication skills with a customer-first mindset. Technical Proficiency: Experience with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, and comfortable learning web-based systems. Problem Solving & Dependability: High level of reliability, attention to detail, and sound judgment during sensitive or urgent situations. Policy Knowledge: Ability to quickly learn and apply Residence Hall Handbook policies and procedures. Additional Information: Residence Life Office Assistant positions are filled throughout the academic year as vacancies occur. Applications will remain active in the hiring pool and will be reviewed as positions become available. Applicants who are no longer interested in employment are encouraged to withdraw their application. Continued employment is contingent upon maintaining all eligibility requirements, satisfactory job performance, and adherence to University and Residence Life policies. Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a diverse, equitable, and inclusive community. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205826": {
      "title": "English - Adjunct Pool for Early College in Greater Worcester, Massachusetts",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: English - Adjunct Pool for Early College in Greater Worcester, Massachusetts Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: English - Adjunct Pool for Early College in Greater Worcester, Massachusetts Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details English - Adjunct Pool for Early College in Greater Worcester, Massachusetts Category: Day and Evening Adjunct Pools Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Oct 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 205826 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a vibrant public university located in the residential west side of Worcester, Massachusetts, the second largest city in New England and home to 38,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Situated on a compact 58-acre campus, the University offers 50 undergraduate and graduate academic programs to more than 6,400 students annually. The Princeton Review ranks us as one of the 75 \"Best Value\" public colleges in the country, as well as a \"Best in the Northeast\" college. Of the 13 undergraduate public universities in the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Worcester State University is one of only three to earn the latter distinction, which is largely based on academic quality and student surveys. Our tag line, \"Change the way the world works,\" speaks to our commitment to graduating students who are not only prepared for work or further study, but who also have learned how they can make a difference. With a marketing slogan of \"Academic excellence at an affordable price,\" the University strives to provide the best academic experience to students from all walks of life. Job Description: The English Department and Early College Program seeks qualified individuals to join our adjunct hiring pool to express their interest in future, part-time teaching assignments at Worcester State. Adjunct faculty members teach 3-credit undergraduate courses, typically at the introductory level.  Faculty with experience teaching first year writing, business communications, and/or technical writing are preferred. Total credits will vary from 3 - 9 in the day division, DGCE, or a combination thereof. Requirements: Master's degree required; Ph.D. preferred. An M.Ed with at least 27+ graduate credits earned in English considered. College teaching experience is preferred. Experience with distance learning preferred. Must have a laptop and reliable internet access. Early College Classes typically meet in-person 2 to 3 times each week for 60 to 90 minutes per class, between 7:30am and 2:05pm at a local high school Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. M/F/D/V. Women and minorities are strongly encouraged to apply. It is the policy of Worcester State University that all employees be vaccinated against COVID-19 before they begin employment. Proof of the COVID-19 vaccine is required of all individuals hired by WSU, to be verified after an offer of employment has been made, and as part of the background check process. Prospective employees may submit a request for exemption based on a religious and/or medical basis, to Human Resources. Application submission to the part time adjunct faculty pool is open to qualified professionals who possess skills, education, and experience in academic and/or professional areas. Early College in Massachusetts is a statewide educational initiative that allows high school students (mostly juniors and seniors) to take strategically sequenced, tuition-free college classes while earning both high school and college credits. Adjunct faculty postings are for potential part-time, non-benefited, teaching positions during the 2020-2021 academic year. The applicant pool will be reviewed by the department chair, when searching for candidates to fill the position. Applicants for adjunct positions will not be notified of their status unless they are contacted by the department chair or their designee. Applicants should withdraw their application from the pool if they are no longer interested. Application Instructions: Please submit a CV, cover-letter (noting interest in day, evening, or both), a list of three professional references, and one letter of reference dated within the last 6 months. Educational background will be verified through the National Student Clearinghouse or through copies of original, sealed transcripts if selected for hire.  Documents which cannot be uploaded to one's account may be sent via fax to 508.929.8169 or by mail to the following address: Director of Human Resources Worcester State University 486 Chandler Street Worcester, MA 01602-2597 Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
