anliness and upkeep of university buildings and building walkways. Responsibilities: (E) = Essential (E) Cleans any/all areas of university buildings including but not limited to offices, classrooms, corridors, walls, floors, windows, furniture, woodwork, toilets, bathrooms, showers, locker rooms, fixtures, etc., by washing, sanitizing, waxing, buffing, sweeping, polishing, dusting, and vacuuming; meets the university's standard for cleanliness in performance of duties. (E) Operates powered cleaning equipment including but not limited to buffers, vacuums, and power washers. (E) Moves furniture and materials in accordance with proper lifting techniques, as necessary. (E) Reviews inventory of cleaning supplies in work area(s) and requests/attains additional supplies as needed. (E) Empties waste receptacles including but not limited to waste barrels, garbage cans, and recycling bins. May be responsible for operating university vehicles and disposing waste in dumpsters. (E) Shovels snow to maintain clear building walkways and stairs; spreads salt and/or sand as necessary. (E) Makes general repairs of a simple nature, including minor repairs to cleaning equipment and replacing light bulbs. (E) Properly secures cleaning equipment, cleaning equipment storage rooms, classrooms, offices, and buildings after use and in accordance with Facilities Operations guidelines. (E) May be responsible for training new Maintainer II employees from time-to-time, as assigned. (E) Inspects assigned work area(s) and notifies supervisor of areas or items requiring attention, such as leaking faucets, broken latches, damaged paint, etc. (E) Periodically inspects cleaning equipment for wear and tear; notifies supervisor of concerns. (E) Assists with delivering goods and moving materials when needed and as assigned. (E) Serves as designated essential personnel; responds to weather and other emergency situations as assigned. (E) Performs all duties safely and responsibly. (E) Demonstrates civility and professional, customer-service oriented behavior, worthy of emulation by other staff and students. (E) Responsible for contributing to the WSU Strategic Plan. (E) Responsible for contributing to Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action objectives. Performs other duties as assigned within the Maintainer classification. Classification specifications are available at http://www.mass.edu/foradmin/humanresources/classspecshrd.asp Requirements: Required Qualifications: Ability to understand and apply the rules, regulations, policies, procedures, specifications, standards, and guidelines governing assigned work. Ability to comprehend and communicate effectively in the English language. Ability to establish and maintain harmonious working relationships. Ability to stand and walk for long periods of time. Ability to lift and carry heavy objects, up to 50 pounds without assistance. Ability to climb and work on ladders and scaffolds. Ability to operate powered and non-powered cleaning equipment. Physical stamina and endurance. Ability to legally operate a motor vehicle; valid drivers' license required. Ability to exercise sound judgment. Ability to work well independently and in a team setting. Ability to work overtime. Ability to perform essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Ability to successfully pass a pre-employment physical, drug test, thorough background check, and CORI check. Preferred Qualifications: Strong work ethic and a willingness to learn. Experience in building custodial work. Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Here at Worcester State University, it is strongly recommended that all employees be vaccinated against COVID-19 before they begin employment. This is a grade 11, non-exempt, full-time (40 hours/week), benefited AFSCME position. The bi-weekly salary is $1,797.80 (annual salary is $46,742.80). The shift is Sunday- Thursday, 6:00am- 2:30pm. Worcester State University offers a competitive benefits package that includes: a choice of 8 different pre-taxed, health insurance plan options pension and supplemental plan retirement options life insurance up to 8x the annual salary long-term disability coverage dental insurance 10 vacation days accrued per year 15 sick days accrued per year 5 personal days per year paid holidays Free on-campus gym access. tuition remission for self, spouse, and dependent children and more... We are an equal opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. M/F/D/V. Members of traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online and may do so by visiting www.worcester.edu/careers, and submitting a cover letter, resume, and the contact information of three professional references. For assistance with uploading materials, log a ticket via the HelpDesk link, or contact us directly at 508-929-8053. URL: www.worcester.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    },
    "https://worcester.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206253": {
      "title": "Health and Wellness Educator (Part-Time, Non-Benefited) 1 Position",
      "description": "Worcester State University\nJob Posting: Health and Wellness Educator (Part-Time, Non-Benefited) 1 Position Worcester State University \n\tJob Posting: Health and Wellness Educator (Part-Time, Non-Benefited) 1 Position Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Health and Wellness Educator (Part-Time, Non-Benefited) 1 Position Category: Grant Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Oct 29, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 206253 Share About Worcester State University: WORCESTER STATE UNIVERSITY is a liberal arts and sciences university with a long tradition of academic excellence dating back to 1874, as well as an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer that seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. Our workforce is dedicated to academic quality, student-centered programming, engaged citizenship, open exchanges of ideas, diversity and inclusiveness, and civility and integrity. We are looking for job applicants who share these values and commitment to our students. Worcester State is centrally located in Massachusetts, about an hour's drive from Boston, Springfield, and Providence, Rhode Island. Our 58-acre campus is nestled in the residential northwest side of Worcester--the second largest city in New England and home to 37,000 college students at more than a dozen colleges and universities. Over 6,000 of those students attend Worcester State--approximately 5,300 are undergraduates and 1,000 are graduate students. Learn more about us at worcester.edu/about . Job Description: Title: Health and Wellness Educator Department: Athletics Supervision Received: Meredith Merchant, Associate Director of Recreation and Wellness General Statement of Duties: The Health and Wellness Educator will assess, plan, implement, supervise and evaluate high quality, effective health and wellness programs and services. The Health Educator will develop innovative educational opportunities for students, coordinate with internal and external stakeholders for programs, and contribute to student success and well-being. Responsibilities: (E) = Essential (E) Plan, implement and evaluate health promotion strategies, policies, programs, and services. (E) Prioritize and coordinate health promotion initiatives based on institutional priorities, identified and emerging student trends, and available resources. (E) Collaborate with campus partners to develop a comprehensive multidisciplinary approach to health and wellness issues for students and campus community. (E) Conduct periodic health and wellness needs assessments of student populations and the campus community. (E) Collect, analyze, and report program participation, learning outcomes, and assessment data to demonstrate program efficacy. (E) Coordinate, implement, and evaluate alcohol and other drug (AOD) prevention and education initiatives in collaboration with campus partners for general and targeted student populations, including first-year students, student-athletes, and other identified groups. (E) Assist with implementation and follow up for online student education programs with a third-party vendor. (E) Develop and implement educational initiatives related to nutrition, body image, disordered eating, and overall wellness. (E) Conduct educational programs on health and wellness issues for general audiences and specific student groups such as residence hall students, commuter, athletic teams, clubs, and organizations. (E) Develop and coordinate health promotion events such as a Wellness Fair. (E) Serve as a campus resource by providing consultation, training, and educational presentations to students, faculty, staff, and campus partners. (E) Identify and assist in pursuing grant opportunities and external funding sources that support health promotion initiatives. (E) Evaluate the effectiveness of all programs related to AOD to improve services and meet the University's required Drug Free Schools and Campuses Regulations.  Assist with the DAAPP annual notification and Biennial Review Report. (E) Assist with the development and maintenance of websites, social media, and health promotion communications related to health and wellness initiatives. (E) Create promotional and educational materials to support health promotion initiatives and campus outreach efforts. Performs other duties as assigned. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Health Education, Health Sciences or related field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum of two (2) years related health promotion work experience Ability to provide leadership and problem-solving skills in analyzing health promotion needs of college students Proficient in a variety of computer software applications Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to effectively interact and work collaboratively with diverse populations of students, staff, faculty, and administrators. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree required in Health Education, Health Sciences or related field. Minimum of two (2) years related health promotion work experience, preferably in a higher education environment Certified Health Education Specialist (CHES); or Certified in Public Health (CPH), with intent to become certified as Health Education Specialist Experience and training in BASICS and Motivational Interviewing Ability to provide leadership and problem-solving skills in analyzing health promotion needs of college students Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to effectively interact and work collaboratively with diverse populations of students, staff, faculty, and administrators. Proficient in a variety of computer software applications Additional Information: Worcester State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer which seeks to reflect the diversity of its community. This is a part-time, non-benefited, hourly position. Hourly Rate: $36 per hour Application Instructions: Applicants must apply online at worcester.interviewexchange.com. A representative from the department will contact individuals for interviews. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Worcester State University 486 Chandler St, Worcester, MA 01602"
    }
  },
